  "name": "TUMOR MUTATION BURDEN (TMB)-590 GENE PANEL",
  "code": "2526",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The TMB status is considered low if the TMB score is lower than 10; intermediate if the TMB score is between 10<br>and 15; and high if the TMB score is larger than 15.<br>Clinical interpretation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Association of high TMB with improved response to immune checkpoint inhibitors such as nivolumab,<br>ipilimumab, pembrolizumab, and atezolizumab in cancer types including non-small cell lung cancer,<br>melanoma, and urothelial carcinoma are noted.</li>\n<li>TMB could be a useful predictive biomarker for response to pembrolizumab therapy in patients with<br>previously treated recurrent or metastatic advanced solid tumors.(1-3).</li>\n<li>The FDA has approved pembrolizumab in all cancers with TMB &gt; 10Mut/Mb based on the findings from the<br>phase 2 KEYNOTE-158 study.</li>\n</ul>",
  "showInterpretation": false,
  "sampleType": "ffpe tissue block",
